{"name":"Chilean Heath","hex":"#f9f7de","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"heath","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A tract of level uncultivated land with sandy soil and scrubby vegetation; heathland.","Any small evergreen shrub of the family Ericaceae.\n\nin Erica spp.\nin Cassiope spp.\nin Daboecia spp.\nin Epacris spp. (Australian heath)\nin Leucopogon spp. (beard heath)\nin Phyllodoce spp. (mountain heath)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heath"}],"entries":[{"title":"Heath","blocks":[{"text":"A heath is a shrubland habitat found mainly on free-draining infertile, acidic soils and is characterised by open, low-growing woody vegetation. Moorland is generally related to high-ground heaths with—especially in Great Britain—a cooler and damper climate."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Amrum_%28187753235%29.jpeg/330px-Amrum_%28187753235%29.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heath","wikidata":"Q27590"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/L%C3%BCneburger_Heide_109.jpg/250px-L%C3%BCneburger_Heide_109.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/L%C3%BCneburger_Heide_109.jpg/500px-L%C3%BCneburger_Heide_109.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/L%C3%BCneburger_Heide_109.jpg/250px-L%C3%BCneburger_Heide_109.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AL%C3%BCneburger_Heide_109.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Fynbos.jpg/250px-Fynbos.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thu